<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soninke</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soninke are a Mande people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, living in the area of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>. They founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a>, also known as Wagadou. Accounts of the Ghana Empire describe the Soninke as the empire's ruling people and traders.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>The Soninke</b> people who built it were iron-working and militarily capable.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Its population included Mandinka, <b>Soninke</b>, Fulani, Songhai and Tuareg communities, which encouraged cultural exchange and bound the outlying regions into one imperial economy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mali-empire">Mali Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The emirs led warrior lineages that took tribute from Berber scholarly tribes, Fulani herders and <b>Soninke</b> and Bambara farmers.</blockquote><a href="/state/awlad-mbarak-emirate">Awlad Mbarak emirate</a></li><li><blockquote>Diarra's <b>Soninke</b> rulers governed a mixed population of farmers and herders and profited from the trade between the desert and the savanna.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-diarra">Kingdom of Diarra</a></li><li><blockquote>Gajaaga was founded by the Bacili clan of <b>Soninke</b> on the upper Senegal around the junction with the Faleme river, an area rich in gold from nearby Bambuk.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-gajaaga">Kingdom of Gajaaga</a></li><li><blockquote>Around 1753 their leader Sebamana established a kingdom in the Sahel country north of the Senegal river, among <b>Soninke</b> and Fulbe communities, eventually with its capital at Nioro.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-kaarta">Kingdom of Kaarta</a></li></ul></section>
